## Setting (classical mathematics, NOT formalized in this file)

X = {F = 0} ⊂ P⁷, F = x₀³ + … + x₇³, S = ℤ[x₀,…,x₇], F_k = ∂F/∂x_k = 3x_k², Jacobian ideal
J = (x₀²,…,x₇²).  So J₇ is spanned by the septic monomials that are not squarefree, and S₇/J₇ has the
basis (x₀⋯x₇)/x_j, j = 0..7: *a septic lies in J₇ iff its 8 "squarefree coefficients" vanish.*
The 3-planes
  P₁ = {x₀+x₁ = x₂+x₃ = x₄+x₅ = x₆+x₇ = 0},   P₂ = {x₀+x₇ = x₁+x₂ = x₃+x₄ = x₅+x₆ = 0}
lie on X and meet in one point.  Their period polynomials are, up to a common constant,
a₁ = ∏ (xᵢ - xⱼ) over the pairs of P₁ and a₂ likewise (period formula for linear cycles).
For the class δ = [P₁] + λ[P₂] put a = a₁ + λa₂.  Along F + tG + t²G₂ the class stays a Hodge class
 * to first order  iff  a·G ∈ J₇;  then write a·G = Σ_k B_k F_k (B_k quintics);
 * to second order (for a suitable G₂)  iff  the class of
       B·∇G - G·div B - l_δ·G²        in  S₇ / (J₇ + a·S₃)
   vanishes (Griffiths–Dwork pole-order reduction; see the note).  Here l_δ = l₁ + λl₂ is a linear
   form; l_i is pinned down by the requirement that B·∇G - G·div B - l_i·G² ∈ J₇ for the cubics G
   vanishing on P_i (those deformations keep the plane, hence the class).

The following are used as input and are NOT proved here: the Griffiths–Dwork reduction and the
order-by-order criterion just stated; the period formula giving a₁, a₂; the whole derivation in the
note — in particular that the displayed class is the obstruction, that it does not depend on the
choice of the B_k, and that one linear form l_i works for ALL cubics through P_i.  (Lean tests 13
explicit cubics per plane.  That l_i = 0 works for every cubic through P_i is checked in exact
arithmetic, by polarisation on 144 generators, in `night/lean_ob/check_all_cubics.py` — Python, not
Lean.)

## What the Lean kernel checks

Everything is a computation with sparse integer polynomials; all definitions are in sections 1–2.
`N3(A, G) = Σ_k B3_k·∂G/∂x_k - G·Σ_k ∂B3_k/∂x_k` with `Σ_k B3_k·x_k² = A`, i.e. B_k = B3_k/3 and N3 is
3 × (B·∇G - G·div B);  `ob3 λ = Λ(N3((a₁+λa₂)·G_λ, G_λ))`, where G_λ = λg₁ - g₂ and Λ is the sum of
